PYTHON LAB 3 - BOUNDED FILE / PROC READ

Create /tmp/proc.py:

  fd = open("/proc/net/wifi", 0)
  if fd < 0:
      print("open failed")
  else:
      data = read(fd, 32)
      print(data)
      close(fd)

Run: python /tmp/proc.py
Expected: a byte-list representation of the first <=32 bytes,
or 'open failed' when that proc node is unavailable.

The Python-like read() yields byte data assigned to a variable, not
normal CPython file objects. Avoid print of huge /proc or /dev nodes.
Use one finite call and close the fd. For raw bytes, read may include
values that are not printable ASCII. Do not call unbounded cat on
streaming GPIO/ADC nodes. See /man/python-examples.
